Given equation of circle x²+y²+2 g x+2 f y+c=0 \quad(c>0) Coordinate of centre $=(-g,-f)\text{ radius }=\sqrt{g^2+f^2-c} \\ Circle touch both$ the $axes, so \begin{aligned} g² & =f²=c \Rightarrow g= \pm \sqrt{c}\\
f \text{ and } = \pm \sqrt{c}
\end{aligned}$ So, coordinate of centre lies in third quadrant so, centre is $(-\sqrt{c},-\sqrt{c})$
equation of given line $x+y+\sqrt{c}=0$
So, line pass through the point of contact to axes of the circle. $\text{ Hence, intercept } \begin{aligned} A B & =\sqrt{(-\sqrt{c}-0)^2+(0+\sqrt{c})^2}\\ \text{ and } =\sqrt{c+c}=\sqrt{2 c}
\end{aligned}$

10940.sol:
Let $P(B)=p$ according to given condition
$\begin{aligned}
P(A) & =2 P(B)=2 p \\
P\left(\frac{R}{A}\right) & =\frac{{ }^3 C_1}{{ }^5 C_1}=\frac{3}{5}
\end{aligned}
and
P\left(\frac{R}{B}\right)=\frac{{ }^4 C_1}{{ }^7 C_1}=\frac{4}{7}$
Using Baye's theorem
$\begin{aligned}
P\left(\frac{B}{R}\right) & =\frac{P(B) \cdot P\left(\frac{R}{B}\right)}{P(A) \cdot P\left(\frac{R}{A}\right)+P(B) \cdot P\left(\frac{R}{B}\right)} \\
& =\frac{p \cdot \frac{4}{7}}{2 p \cdot \frac{3}{5}+p \cdot \frac{4}{7}} \\
& =\frac{\frac{4}{7}}{\frac{6}{5}+\frac{4}{7}}=\frac{\frac{4}{7}}{\frac{42+20}{35}} \\
& =\frac{20}{62}=\frac{10}{31}
\end{aligned}$

